  "headnote_district_ruling": "Judge Chesler dismissed municipalities’ putative class action seeking franchise fees from Netflix and Hulu under the New Jersey Cable Television Act.",
  "qualification_rationale": "The case resolved a novel and economically significant attempt to apply legacy cable-franchise statutes to internet streaming services and to let municipalities enforce the statute directly.",
  "appellate_posture_note": "The Third Circuit affirmed in a precedential opinion, holding that the Act does not imply a municipal private right of action. Because that resolved the case, the court did not need to decide whether Netflix or Hulu is substantively a cable television company under the Act.",
